The recurrence is exact in mathematics, and there is no step size and no truncation. But \(1/3\) and \(10/3\) are stored rounded, which adds a tiny multiple of the other solution, \(3^n\). That part grows by a factor 3 per step while the true solution shrinks by a factor 3, so after 15 steps the two are of similar size and after 30 steps the computed value is wrong by a factor of \(10^{11}\). This is instability: an algorithm that amplifies rounding error. (Running the recurrence backwards, from large \(n\) down, is stable.)









